WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.580
10 open moly models swing sparsity from four times to 128 times, changing which GPUs builders can use. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 228, a channel mixing time series net, a gift-avel bakeoff of foundation forecasters, agents against national lab questions, then things to try. DeepSeek V4 Pro, in a mark-tech post audit of open mixture of experts or moly, models taken from hugging face can fig JSON files,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:36.640
and Technical Reports, uses 384 experts with square soft plus gating and hash routing in 3 layers,

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.580
matching Kimi K2 at the top of a range that starts at 8 experts in Mixtrol.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.960
Top-K selection, the count of experts allowed to fire, runs from one in Lama 4 Maverick,

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.820
whose gating method stays undisclosed, to 8 in several Quinn and Kimi variants.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:59.080
Deepseek V3 and later variants drop the usual auxiliary loss for an ox-loss-free bias,

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:03.420
that steers which expert is chosen and leaves the mixing weights untouched.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:09.940
Kimmy K2 showed that raising sparsity from 8 to 48 cut floating-point operations or flops

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:13.720
by 1.69 times at identical validation loss.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:19.160
A companion guide out the same day walks through the seven routing strategies in production use

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:25.460
an auditable reference for whether a given MoE will run on a single 80 gigabyte graphics processing unit

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:30.040
or GPU, or needs expert parallelism across multiple cards.

00:01:30.862 --> 00:01:36.342
On the machine learning subreddit, GRFnet is a pie-torch model for multi-channel time-series

00:01:36.342 --> 00:01:41.522
classification that mixes input channels with learned spatial filters initialized from

00:01:41.522 --> 00:01:46.462
electrode positions when available, then sends the result through a bank of mostly frozen

00:01:46.462 --> 00:01:47.762
dilated convolutions.

00:01:48.282 --> 00:01:55.222
It extracts summary statistics, gates them, and classifies with a 3,847 parameter head on

00:01:55.222 --> 00:02:01.062
the default 22-channel 4-class setting, accepts variable-length inputs and adapts to sampling

00:02:01.062 --> 00:02:08.542
rate without retraining. A subject-independent evaluation on PhysioNet EEG MMIDB is underway

00:02:08.542 --> 00:02:17.065
against EEGNet and shallow-convNet. Comparing TimeStrawl, T0, Tabby, and Morpheus 2.0 on GIFT

00:02:17.065 --> 00:02:23.345
Aval, towards data science shows all 4-time series foundation models scale, patch, and output

00:02:23.345 --> 00:02:28.465
quantiles. The decisive difference is how each series shares information across the batch.

00:02:28.945 --> 00:02:33.725
An architectural split between treating series independently and borrowing statistical strength

00:02:33.725 --> 00:02:39.049
from one another during training. Shape naming in one room, two room, and three room,

00:02:39.169 --> 00:02:44.429
3D environments is now a locally trained VLA models job on the machine learning subreddit.

00:02:44.869 --> 00:02:51.929
A 25.5 million parameter recurrent network that keeps a 768 by 768 state matrix

00:02:51.929 --> 00:03:06.689
with Purcell long short-term memory, or LSTM style gates and learns visual attention directly over raw 128 by 128 red-green blue, or RGB pixels, without a separate pre-trained encoder.

00:03:07.209 --> 00:03:19.969
It was transitioned from a language modeling checkpoint and reaches more than 90%, more than 80%, and more than 60% success respectively on randomized test runs of those 1, 2, and 3-room tasks.

00:03:19.969 --> 00:03:25.649
training use supervised imitation on 70,000 steps with batch size 4 after an

00:03:25.649 --> 00:03:31.561
initial 150,000 language modeling steps. Autonomous agents tried open research

00:03:31.561 --> 00:03:36.681
questions from US national lab problem lists. The decoder found and none of the

00:03:36.681 --> 00:03:41.241
nine cleared the bar domain expert set. The evaluation asked whether they could

00:03:41.241 --> 00:03:46.497
form, run and check novel research steps with no human in the loop. Law firms

00:03:46.497 --> 00:03:51.577
already by malpractice coverage for human associates, and the New York Times examines whether

00:03:51.577 --> 00:03:56.797
those policies cover errors by AI agents that draft contracts, perform due diligence,

00:03:57.117 --> 00:04:02.037
or manage discovery, and how liability should attach when the agent sits inside the firm's

00:04:02.037 --> 00:04:02.417
workflow.

00:04:03.137 --> 00:04:05.137
Amazon Quick released a taxonomy.

00:04:05.777 --> 00:04:10.277
